        "id": 14810,
        "name": "Chrono",
        "username": "Chrono",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chrono/{size}/2334_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-15T14:23:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was working on story ideas for the RPG and noticed that the book that gave citizens Blood, Sweat, and Tears their powers is called the Fabric of Despair. There is also a set of 4 comic books with that same title quoted from for card references in Gloomweaver's deck, including both of Cult Leader Massey's quotes.</p><p>So were Blood, Sweat, and Tears members of the Gloomweaver cult before they became citizens? Or did they find the book, change, and then Cult Leader Massey got the book from them? Or is it all just a coincidence?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:59.964Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
