        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"Chrono\"]\n\nI was working on story ideas for the RPG and noticed that the book that gave citizens Blood, Sweat, and Tears their powers is called the Fabric of Despair. There is also a set of 4 comic books with that same title quoted from for card references in Gloomweaver&#39;s deck, including both of Cult Leader Massey&#39;s quotes.So were Blood, Sweat, and Tears members of the Gloomweaver cult before they became citizens? Or did they find the book, change, and then Cult Leader Massey got the book from them? Or is it all just a coincidence?\n\n[/quote]\n\nConsidering they called themselves the corpse covonant and were pretty gothy kids, it would make a lot of sense to me that they had dealings with the Cult of Gloom just based on who they were as people. And it would seem rather odd to me if they got their hands on a major Cult of Gloom text without being somewhat close to them ya know? I have no idea if they were actually ever official members, but it wouldnt surprise me if they ran around in the same circles\n",
